WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.482
Arithmetic lets us turn raw values into useful metrics.

00:00:04.482 --> 00:00:07.737
Sales minus costs gives profit.

00:00:07.737 --> 00:00:11.377
Profit divided by sales can give a margin.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:14.962
Profit minus tax can give net profit.

00:00:14.962 --> 00:00:19.586
These are derived metrics because they are created from other values.

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:28.573
Python uses familiar operators: plus for addition, minus for subtraction, an asterisk for multiplication,

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:33.623
a forward slash for division, and two asterisks for exponentiation.

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:37.403
The formula matters more than the syntax.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:42.223
Python can run a perfectly valid calculation that represents the wrong business idea,

00:00:42.223 --> 00:00:48.373
so always understand the meaning of the metric before trusting the result.
